  "summary_en": "Nevada statute chapter governing testing and operation of autonomous vehicles on state highways. It defines automation levels via SAE J3016 and sets insurance or bond requirements, human operator and minimal-risk-condition rules, crash reporting, manufacturer liability limits, state preemption of local regulation, and penalties.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Testing requires $5,000,000 insurance, self-insurance, or bond.",
   "Non-fully autonomous vehicles need a human operator able to take control; fully autonomous ones must achieve a minimal risk condition on failure.",
   "Crashes during testing with injury or damage over $750 must be reported within 10 business days.",
   "Original manufacturers are not liable for defects from unauthorized third-party conversion or modification.",
   "Only the DMV may regulate AV technology; local governments cannot impose taxes, fees or requirements."
  ],
